        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "AZLX-23-001045 - Amazon Linux 2023 must monitor remote access methods."
          info        : "Remote access services, such as those providing remote access to network devices and information systems, which lack automated monitoring capabilities, increase risk and make remote user access management difficult at best."
          solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to monitor all remote access methods by installing rsyslog with the following command:

$ sudo yum install rsyslog

Then add or update the following lines to the \"/etc/rsyslog.conf\" file:

auth.*;authpriv.*;daemon.* /var/log/secure

The \"rsyslog\" service must be restarted for the changes to take effect. To restart the \"rsyslog\" service, run the following command:

$ sudo systemctl restart rsyslog.service"
