    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "AZLX-23-002555 - Amazon Linux 2023 debug-shell systemd service must be disabled."
      info        : "The debug-shell requires no authentication and provides root privileges to anyone who has physical access to the machine. While this feature is disabled by default, masking it adds an additional layer of assurance that it will not be enabled via a dependency in systemd. This also prevents attackers with physical access from trivially bypassing security on the machine through valid troubleshooting configurations and gaining root access when the system is rebooted."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to mask the debug-shell systemd service with the following command:

$ sudo systemctl disable --now debug-shell.service
$ sudo systemctl mask --now debug-shell.service"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.7,800-171r3|03.01.07a.,800-53|AC-6(10),800-53r5|AC-6(10),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-002235,CN-L3|7.1.3.2(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.2(g),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(d),CN-L3|8.1.10.6(a),CSF|PR.AC-4,CSF2.0|PR.AA-05,DISA_Benchmark|Amazon_Linux_2023_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.18,ITSG-33|AC-6,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.2.2,NESA|T5.4.1,NESA|T5.4.4,NESA|T5.4.5,NESA|T5.5.4,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NIAv2|AM1,NIAv2|AM23f,NIAv2|SS13c,NIAv2|SS15c,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|7.1.2,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.1,PCI-DSSv4.0|7.2.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,Rule-ID|SV-274173r1120507_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002555,SWIFT-CSCv1|5.1,TBA-FIISB|31.4.2,TBA-FIISB|31.4.3,Vuln-ID|V-274173"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Amazon_Linux_2023_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      cmd         : "/bin/systemctl status debug-shell.service | /bin/awk '{print} END {if(NR==0) print \"No results found\" }'"
      expect      : "(^[\\s]*Loaded:[\\s]*[Mm]asked|No results found)"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "AZLX-23-002565 - Amazon Linux 2023 must synchronize internal information system clocks to the authoritative time source at least every 24 hours."
      info        : "Inaccurate time stamps make it more difficult to correlate events and can lead to an inaccurate analysis. Determining the correct time a particular event occurred on a system is critical when conducting forensic analysis and investigating system events. Sources outside the configured acceptable allowance (drift) may be inaccurate.

Synchronizing internal information system clocks provides uniformity of time stamps for information systems with multiple system clocks and systems connected over a network.

Depending on the infrastructure in use, the \"pool\" directive may not be supported.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000356-GPOS-00144, SRG-OS-000785-GPOS-00250, SRG-OS-000359-GPOS-00146"
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to compare internal information system clocks at least every 24 hours with an NTP server. Ensure the following line is added or updated in \"/etc/chrony.conf\":

server <USNO/DOD Server> iburst maxpoll 16"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.7,800-171r3|03.03.07b.,800-53|AU-8b.,800-53r5|AU-8b.,800-53r5|SC-45,800-53r5|SC-45(1)(a),800-53r5|SC-45(1)(b),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001890,CCI|CCI-004922,CCI|CCI-004923,CCI|CCI-004926,CN-L3|8.1.4.3(b),CSF|PR.PT-1,DISA_Benchmark|Amazon_Linux_2023_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.17,ITSG-33|AU-8,NESA|T3.6.7,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-274175r1190705_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002565,TBA-FIISB|37.4,Vuln-ID|V-274175"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Amazon_Linux_2023_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      file        : "/etc/chrony.conf"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*server[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]+$"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*server[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+maxpoll[\\s]+([1-9]|1[0-6])([\\s].*)?$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "AZLX-23-002575 - Amazon Linux 2023 must prevent the loading of a new kernel for later execution."
      info        : "Changes to any software components can have significant effects on the overall security of Amazon Linux 2023. This requirement ensures the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor.

All software packages must be signed with a cryptographic key recognized and approved by the organization.

Verifying the authenticity of software prior to installation validates the integrity of the software package received from a vendor. This verifies the software has not been tampered with and that it has been provided by a trusted vendor."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 to disable kernel image loading.

Add or edit the following line in a system configuration file in the \"/etc/sysctl.d/\" directory:

kernel.kexec_load_disabled = 1

Load settings from all system configuration files with the following command:

$ sudo sysctl --system"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.5,800-171r3|03.04.05,800-53|CM-5(3),800-53r5|CM-14,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-003992,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|Amazon_Linux_2023_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.2,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.4,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.19,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.31,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.32,ITSG-33|CM-5(3),NESA|T3.2.3,NESA|T5.1.1,NESA|T5.6.1,NESA|T7.5.1,NESA|T7.5.3,NESA|T7.6.3,QCSC-v1|7.2,Rule-ID|SV-274177r1120519_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002575,Vuln-ID|V-274177"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Amazon_Linux_2023_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      cmd         : "/usr/sbin/sysctl kernel.kexec_load_disabled"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*kernel\\.kexec_load_disabled[\\s]*=[\\s]*1[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "AZLX-23-002580 - Amazon Linux 2023 must prevent files with the setuid and setgid bit set from being executed on the /boot/efi directory."
      info        : "The \"nosuid\" mount option causes the system not to execute \"setuid\" and \"setgid\" files with owner privileges. This option must be used for mounting any file system not containing approved \"setuid\" and \"setguid\" files. Executing files from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for nonprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 so that the /boot/efi directory is mounted with the \"nosuid\" option.

Modify \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nosuid\" option on the \"/boot/efi\" directory."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-53|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(2),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|Amazon_Linux_2023_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7(2),NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-274178r1120522_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002580,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-274178"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Amazon_Linux_2023_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot/efi[\\s]+"
      expect      : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/boot/efi[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]+nosuid"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "AZLX-23-002585 - Amazon Linux 2023 must mount /dev/shm with the nodev option."
      info        : "The \"nodev\" mount option causes the system to not interpret character or block special devices. Executing character or block special devices from untrusted file systems increases the opportunity for nonprivileged users to attain unauthorized administrative access."
      solution    : "Configure Amazon Linux 2023 so that \"/dev/shm\" is mounted with the \"nodev\" option.

Modify \"/etc/fstab\" to use the \"nodev\" option on the \"/dev/shm\" file system."
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.7,800-171r3|03.04.06,800-53|CM-7(2),800-53r5|CM-7(2),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001764,CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF|PR.PT-3,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|Amazon_Linux_2023_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ITSG-33|CM-7(2),NIAv2|SS15a,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|2.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,Rule-ID|SV-274179r1120525_rule,STIG-ID|AZLX-23-002585,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-274179"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Amazon_Linux_2023_V1R4_STIG.zip"
      file        : "/etc/fstab"
      regex       : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/dev/shm[\\s]"
      expect      : "^[^#\\n\\r]+[\\s]+/dev/shm[\\s]+[^#\\n\\r]*nodev"
      required    : NO
    </custom_item>

